  "description": "The types the daemon source declares outside cmd/, proxy/, wrap/ and zazz/ (which have their own diagrams). Engine is the shared state every front end and command uses, including the zazz state declared in zazz/; Store, WalkCache and Sessions are its caches; Stored is an output read back from the output store; Request is the wire message; Backend lets the MCP server be tested without a daemon; Pool and Arena are per-process and per-thread machinery for parallel work and tree-sitter parses; the modules Store and its Entry lines describe downloadable language modules, and tools.rs (which declares no type) uses the same Store for JIT tools such as ai-agent; Cli::Llm is `zazzle daemon llm`; Reply and Ran are a local model answer and a finished ai-agent run (llm.rs), and Section is one rule section or skill a brief offers the model (brief.rs). testutil.rs (tests only) is left out.",
